<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="56939" href="schedule/2012/spring/SCAN/496/56939.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2012" href="schedule/2012.xml">2012</calendarYear><term id="120121" href="schedule/2012/spring.xml">Spring 2012</term><subject id="SCAN" href="schedule/2012/spring/SCAN.xml">Scandinavian</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2012/spring/SCAN/496.xml">Special Topics in Scan Studies</course></parents><sectionNumber>MS3</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Special Topics: Kierkegaard</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Meets with CWL 441and PHIL 444.  TOPIC: Kierkegaard &amp; Company: Existentialism, Pietism and The Discovery of Self   Beginning with philosophical questions posed by Soren Kierkegaard in the early 1800s, this course traces themes of existentialism, pietism, individualism and modern notions of "self" as they evolved in Scandinavian literature.  Includes works by Fredrika Bremer, H.C. Andersen, August Strindberg, Henrik Ibsen, Karen Blixen, and Ingmar Bergman.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2012-01-17Z</startDate><endDate>2012-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G48</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Safstrom" firstName="M">Safstrom, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>